<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30717" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nĕmŏrensis</span></b> , e,
			adj.
		nemus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to a grove</i> or <i>wood</i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen. mel, <i><span class="en">Col. 9, 4,
			7</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			In partic. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>Of</i> or <i>belonging to the grove of
				Diana, near Aricia</i>, <i><span class="en">Prop. 3</span></i> (4), 22, 25; cf. <i><span class="en">Ov. F. 3,
				261</span></i>, Vitr 4, 7—Hence: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rex Nemorensis,</span>”
				<i>the presider over the sacrifices to Diana of
					Aricia</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Calig 35</span></i>
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nĕmŏrense</span></b> , is,
				n., <i>a villa of Cæsar, near
				the Arician grove</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Att.
				6, 1, 25</span></i>, in Nemorensi, <i><span class="en">Suet.
				Caes. 46</span></i>; cf. nemus I. B.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
